description:
Start only after D2 in canary-impact-05-shadow-watch is recorded as promote.

Wire the canary-impact selector and test jobs into ci-required-result so a canary regression cannot merge:
- the umbrella requires the test shards whenever the selector reports a non-empty selection;
- the umbrella fails if the selector job fails, or its output is missing, malformed, or inconsistent with the shard results;
- a recorded zero selection is a pass;
- remove the jobs' continue-on-error.

No ruleset change is needed: ci-required-result is already the required check.

DECISION POINT D3 (maintainer, optional): whether to also run the selector on pull_request for earlier feedback. Default is merge_group only, matching the heavy tier; only extend it with an explicit recorded decision.
